      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "### Environment\n\nESLint Playground\n\n### What parser are you using?\n\nDefault (Espree)\n\n### What did you do?\n\n### Playground Code\n```js\nconst f = (function() {\n    class C {\n        field = this.x;\n    }\n}).bind(this);\n```\n\n### ESLint Configuration \n<details> \n <summary> Tap to see full config </summary> \n\n```js\nimport { defineConfig } from \"eslint/config\";\n\nexport default defineConfig([\n    {\n        \"rules\": {\n            \"no-extra-bind\": [\n                \"error\"\n            ]\n        },\n        \"languageOptions\": {\n            \"ecmaVersion\": \"latest\",\n            \"sourceType\": \"module\"\n        }\n    }\n]);\n```\n </details>\n\n\n### What did you expect to happen?\n\nESLint should report `\"The function binding is unnecessary.\"`.\nThe outer functions don't use `this` in their own scope \u2014 the `this` inside class fields and static blocks belongs to the class itself (instance for fields, constructor for static blocks), not the enclosing function. So `.bind(this)` on the outer function is redundant.\n\n\n### What actually happened?\n\nNo problem is reported.\n\n### Link to Minimal Reproducible Example\n\nhttps://eslint.org/play/#eyJ0ZXh0IjoiY29uc3QgZiA9IChmdW5jdGlvbigpIHtcbiAgICBjbGFzcyBDIHtcbiAgICAgICAgZmllbGQgPSB0aGlzLng7XG4gICAgfVxufSkuYmluZCh0aGlzKTsiLCJvcHRpb25zIjp7InJ1bGVzIjp7Im5vLWV4dHJhLWJpbmQiOlsiZXJyb3IiXX0sImxhbmd1YWdlT3B0aW9ucyI6eyJlY21hVmVyc2lvbiI6ImxhdGVzdCIsInNvdXJjZVR5cGUiOiJtb2R1bGUifX19\n\n### Participation\n\n- [x] I am willing to submit a pull request for this issue.\n\n### AI acknowledgment\n\n- [x] I did not use AI to generate this issue report.\n- [ ] (If the above is not checked) I have reviewed the AI-generated content before submitting.\n\n### Additional comments\n\nThe same issue occurs with static blocks",
