      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "### Environment\n\nESLint Playground\n\n### What parser are you using?\n\nDefault (Espree)\n\n### What did you do?\n\n### Playground Code\n```js\nlet flag = false;\n\nconst cb = () => {\n    flag = true;\n};\n\nwhile (flag === false) {\n    cb();\n}\n```\n\n### ESLint Configuration \n<details> \n <summary> Tap to see full config </summary> \n\n```js\nimport { defineConfig } from \"eslint/config\";\n\nexport default defineConfig([\n    {\n        \"rules\": {\n            \"no-unmodified-loop-condition\": [\n                \"error\"\n            ]\n        }\n    }\n]);\n```\n </details>\n\n### ESLint Output\n```\n7:8 'flag' is not modified in this loop. (no-unmodified-loop-condition)\n```\n\n\n### What did you expect to happen?\n\nNo errors. flag is modified inside `cb`, and `cb()` is called in the loop body. The rule already handles this exact pattern when the callback is a function declaration:\n```js\nlet flag = false;\n\nfunction cb() {\n    flag = true;\n}\n\nwhile (flag === false) {  // no error, as expected\n    cb();\n}\n```\n### What actually happened?\n\n7:8 'flag' is not modified in this loop. (no-unmodified-loop-condition)\n\n### Link to Minimal Reproducible Example\n\nhttps://eslint.org/play/#\n\n### Participation\n\n- [x] I am willing to submit a pull request for this issue.\n\n### AI acknowledgment\n\n- [x] I did not use AI to generate this issue report.\n- [ ] (If the above is not checked) I have reviewed the AI-generated content before submitting.\n\n### Additional comments\n\nThis was actually raised back in 2016 in #7192, where @mysticatea confirmed the inconsistency and said \"I think we can expand the support to function expressions and arrows\". It was marked as an enhancement, but was closed after 21 days without reaching consensus. I'm happy to pick it up.",
