      "body": "### Environment\nNode version: v24.15.0\nnpm version: v11.12.1\nLocal ESLint version: v10.7.0\nGlobal ESLint version: Not found\nOperating System: win32 10.0.26200\n\n\n### What parser are you using?\n\nDefault (Espree)\n\n### What did you do?\n\n<details>\n<summary>Configuration</summary>\n\n```js\n{\n  \"rules\": {\n    \"prefer-object-spread\": \"error\"\n  }\n}\n```\n</details>\n\n```js\nconst result = doSomething()\nObject.assign({}, myData)\n\n```\n\n\n### What did you expect to happen?\n\nThe autofix should insert a preceding semicolon to prevent ASI issues, producing:\n```js\nconst result = doSomething()\n;({ ...myData })\n```\n\n\n\n### What actually happened?\n\nThe autofixer transformed the code into this:\n\n```js\nconst result = doSomething()\n({ ...myData })\n```\n\nThis merges the two statements into a single function call, causing a runtime `TypeError`.\n\n### Link to Minimal Reproducible Example\n\nhttps://eslint.org/play/#eyJ0ZXh0IjoiY29uc3QgcmVzdWx0ID0gZG9Tb21ldGhpbmcoKVxuT2JqZWN0LmFzc2lnbih7fSwgbXlEYXRhKVxuIiwib3B0aW9ucyI6eyJydWxlcyI6eyJwcmVmZXItb2JqZWN0LXNwcmVhZCI6WyJlcnJvciJdfSwibGFuZ3VhZ2VPcHRpb25zIjp7InBhcnNlck9wdGlvbnMiOnsiZWNtYUZlYXR1cmVzIjp7fX19fX0=\n\n### Participation\n\n- [x] I am willing to submit a pull request for this issue.\n\n### AI acknowledgment\n\n- [x] I did not use AI to generate this issue report.\n- [ ] (If the above is not checked) I have reviewed the AI-generated content before submitting.\n\n### Additional comments\n\n_No response_",
